https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LWVdKv4-CEg  (Capo 2) (MC2)

Originally done uncapo'd in (D) which includes the (B) so here it is in (C) with easier chords with capo 2.  Now this is how to write a country song.  Larry and Sandy change keys twice without inserting half-step sharps that seemed to be the trendy thing to do in the 70's.  And then the Bryants come along and sue them (and win!) for saying the song sounds too much like Rocky Top?  Nonsense.  Sometimes you'll see a co-writing credit for the Bryants but not in my world.  

TIP:  For the intro, cover the 6th string bass <c> for the first (C/G), then lift off the pinky for a regular (C) but give strings 6 and 5 a good thump for both the (C/G) and the (C).  Then comes  the (F), followed by two single strums, first of an |Fsus| in which you just sneak your pinky under your ring finger without breaking the (F) form.  Lift off for the second (F).  Repeat.
 

